"Model: exact special relativity at any speed. The wire is two infinitely long, thin lines of charge: ions with density +λ₀ at rest in the lab, and electrons drifting at v with density −λ₀ in the lab, so the lab sees a neutral wire. In any frame, each line's density is its density in its own rest frame times its γ in that frame. Fields of an infinite line: E = λ/({#}πε₀r), B = μ₀I/({#}πr). The force is the Lorentz force q(E + u × B) on the test charge. Ignored: the test charge's own field and radiation, the wire's resistance, and the small surface charges that push current around a real circuit.",
"What is drawn: with speeds near c each dot stands for {#} nC of charge (λ₀ × {#} cm), {#} of each kind per {#} cm in the lab; their spacing shows each line's density in the frame drawn. The charges are points, so only their spacing contracts. The ticks mark each line's own spacing, in its rest frame: the ions' is the lab spacing, the electrons' is γᵥ times wider (in the lab their spacing equals the ions', contracted from their own). The contraction control exaggerates only the drawing: drawn spacing = lab spacing × (true spacing ratio)<sup>k</sup>, for the dots and the ticks alike; at ×{#} the drawing is true. Counts and all other numbers are always exact. Distances are to scale (the wire is drawn much thicker than a line). Time is slowed: {#} ns of the frame's own time per second on screen. The test charge, an electron or positron, follows the exact relativistic equation of motion dp/dt = q(E + v × B), computed separately in each frame (RK4, {#} ps steps); its own field and its radiation (about {#}⁻¹⁵ of its energy) are ignored. 3D draws the wire as a cutaway copper wire {#} mm thick on supports {#} cm apart in the lab (at rest there like the ions, so their spacing and width are drawn with the same contraction), over a bench; Flat draws the plain schematic. In the real wire the true spacing, one electron per {#}⁻²³ m of wire, and its {#}⁻²⁶ change cannot be drawn: equal spacing is the honest picture, and the charge is not set free.",
"Model: the exact field of a charge that has moved at constant velocity forever (Heaviside, {#}). It points straight away from where the charge is now: E = kq({#} − β²)/(r²({#} − β² sin²θ)^{#}/{#}), with θ measured from the direction of motion, and B = v × E/c². No acceleration, so no radiation. The view rides with the charge; the grid below is at rest in the lab and slides past at the charge's speed, slowed for the screen. Field lines are spaced so their density shows |E|.",
"Model: the magnet is a uniformly magnetized cylinder, which is the same as a sheet of current K = M around its side. Its field is the exact field of each current loop (complete elliptic integrals), summed along the length by Gauss–Legendre quadrature, {#} nodes; the flux through the ring uses the exact mutual inductance of coaxial loops. Everything moves along the axis at constant speed; fields in the loop's frame come from the exact Lorentz transformation, at everyday speeds too. The EMFs are sums of the push on the charges over {#} pieces of the ring; −dΦ′/dt′ is a central difference. Ignored: the field of the induced current itself (a thin ring of high resistance). The motion on screen is slowed, and near c the magnet and spacing are drawn contracted by γ.",
